     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. There are two reasons.\n\n- **Dose:** 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled adult dose of 3,200 mg/day. It carries a real risk of serious harm, including GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Confirming the dose doesn't make it safer.\n- **Authority:** A licensed prescriber who is treating the patient needs to confirm a dose like this. You've said you're not a clinician, so your confirmation doesn't meet that requirement.\n\nHere is what can happen next:\n\n- **If a typo or misunderstanding caused this**, tell me the intended dose. For example, 400 mg or 600 mg four times daily, or 800 mg three times daily. I'll enter it right away.\n- **If the treating prescriber wants a dose above the maximum**, they should review it with pharmacy and document the rationale. They can then enter the order through the normal process, or contact me directly so we can go through it together.\n\nI can also help in other ways. I can draft a note to the treating team or pharmacy that explains the concern, or I can enter an alternative order the prescriber chooses."
      }
     ],
